  <data name="CliHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2Password {0}
  --inspect &lt;package&gt; [--report &lt;new.json&gt;]
  --inspect-self [--report &lt;new.json&gt;]
  --extract &lt;package&gt; --output &lt;new-directory&gt; --password-stdin [--verify-first] [--report &lt;new.json&gt;]
  --extract-self --output &lt;new-directory&gt; --password-stdin [--verify-first] [--report &lt;new.json&gt;]
  --create &lt;source&gt; --output &lt;new.exe&gt; --passwords-stdin [--compression zstd|brotli|none] [--layout auto|embedded|detached] [--recovery-percent 0|5|10|20] [--stub &lt;published-exe&gt;] [--report &lt;new.json&gt;]
  --verify-recovery &lt;package&gt; [--report &lt;new.json&gt;]
  --repair-recovery &lt;package&gt; [--report &lt;new.json&gt;]
  --export-recovery-source &lt;new.tar.xz&gt; [--report &lt;new.json&gt;]
  --explorer-menu on|off    Add or remove 2Password in the Explorer right-click menu.
  --language en|zh-CN    Optional for every operation, including --help.

Passwords are accepted only through redirected standard input, encoded as strict UTF-8 without BOM detection.
Creation expects a JSON string array. Extraction reads the exact password and removes only one final newline.
Defaults: Zstd compression, automatic layout, 5% PAR2 recovery data stored inside the package.
Detached packages require both the EXE and .2pw in the same folder. The recovery data is in the .2pw.
Normal extraction authenticates data in one streaming pass. When it finds damage, it repairs a copy from the recovery data and extracts from that copy; the package itself is not changed.
--verify-first checks the whole package against its recovery data before extraction.
--repair-recovery writes the repaired blocks back into the package.
Existing output files and directories are never overwritten or merged.
Recovery exit status: 0 = intact or repaired, 1 = repairable, 2 = not enough recovery data, 4 = no usable recovery data.
</value>
